Budget: N = 8, from design_constraints.json (`schematic_sizing_iterations`), NOT
overridden by the caller. Converged at 6, so ONE iteration (7) went unspent --
stop condition 1, not budget exhaustion. Nothing was cut short.

THE THREE MOVES THAT MATTERED, and why:
  1. LENGTH (iter 1, +29.8 dB). Every one of the nine devices arrived at
     l = 0.15 um, the sky130 minimum -- the worst intrinsic gain the process
     offers, on every device at once. gm/gds went 7.8-24.6 to 88-96. It also
     FIXED THE MIRROR: at minimum length, channel-length modulation had broken
     the ratio badly (XMN3/XMN4 measured 0.258 against its geometric 0.400),
     and lengthening restored it while costing almost no gm, because the nfets
     sit at gm/id ~ 23-26 where gm tracks current rather than W/L.
  2. THE NULLING RESISTOR (iter 2, +24.5 deg of PM for zero current). R0 arrived
     at 100 ohm against 1/gm2 = 460 ohm -- 4.6x under-sized, so the RHP zero was
     not being cancelled at all. Sized ABOVE 1/gm2 it becomes an LHP zero near
     the output pole. The single cheapest move in the run.
  3. THE BIAS LEG (iter 3, -34% power). The self-biased reference was burning
     118.6 uA -- 36% of the entire supply -- to produce a 43 uA tail. Cutting
     MP4_W redirected that overhead; it is why the design finishes 34% under
     its power ceiling instead of over it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE MIRROR TIE  (the property this run was built to test)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HELD, end to end, with no intervention.

  XMN4 net7 net7 VSS VSS sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 l=0.4 w=47.2 nf=1 m=5
  XMN3 net3 net7 VSS VSS sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 l=0.4 w=47.2 nf=1 m=2
  XMN5 vout net7 VSS VSS sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 l=0.4 w=47.2 nf=1 m=6
  XMP1 net4 net4 VDD VDD sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 l=0.4 w=14.4 nf=1 m=1
  XMP2 net5 net4 VDD VDD sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 l=0.4 w=14.4 nf=1 m=1

One shared w and one shared l per family, differing only in m. This was never
enforced by vigilance: MN4_W/MN4_L each write all three nfet legs BY
CONSTRUCTION in two_stage_rz_tunable.sp.j2, so no --set could have separated
them and no iteration ever produced a leg with its own width.
(For contrast, the run under the old contract, test_miller_ota_0907, finished
at w = 47.2 / 85 / 100 um on one gate net.)

