--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT A FURTHER RUN WOULD NEED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NO FURTHER SIZING RUN IS NEEDED. Every key of the real spec is met, every key of
the harder spec is met, and the design sits 34% under its power ceiling. There
is no unmet obligation to discharge.

If a future pass is wanted anyway, the honest ranking of what is left:
  * MORE UGBW MARGIN is the only thing worth buying, and it is NOT free. The
    cheap lever is spent: Cc is already down to 36x36 from 45x45, and shrinking
    it further trades PM at about -37 deg per natural-log of UGBW (measured,
    iterations 3->4), so PM would reach its harder floor of 52 at roughly
    18.5 MHz. Past that the only route is more gm1, i.e. more tail current.
  * MORE TAIL CURRENT IS NOT A ONE-VARIABLE MOVE -- iteration 5 proved this
    empirically and it is the most useful finding in the log. XMP3's gate (net5)
    and XMP1/XMP2's gate (net4) sit at the same DC level in balance, so
        I_XMP3 = I_XMP1 * (W/L)_XMP3 / (W/L)_XMP1 = 8.333 * I_tail / 2
    and vout only sits mid-rail when XMN5 sinks exactly that. Raising MN3_M
    2->3 without raising MN5_M put XMP3 into triode (vds 0.090 < vdsat 0.128,
    gm/gds collapsed 74.9 -> 2.0) and cost 25 dB of gain. Any future tail rise
    must move MN3_M and MN5_M TOGETHER, keeping m5/m3 ~ 3. The 1.5x version
    costs about 0.53 mW -- 40% more power for ~1 MHz -- which is why it was
    rejected here rather than pursued.
  * ROUGH COST: 2-3 iterations to re-land a 1.5x-current variant, arriving near
    22 MHz UGBW at ~0.53 mW. Only worth it if post-layout UGBW actually falls
    below 15 MHz. Wait for a real PEX number before spending it.

NOTHING IS JUDGED UNREACHABLE. spec_analysis.log flagged the SET as MODERATELY
CONSTRAINED and pre-registered a STOP test: "if gm/gds is saturated at the l in
force AND PM is driven to the bottom of its range and a key is still short, the
target is over-constrained." Neither condition was reached -- gm/gds is 48-107
with more length available, and PM finished mid-window at 56.96. The spec was
comfortably reachable on this topology with the mirror tied.
